# Browser & visual verification (on demand)

Default: **no browser automation.** Use only when the user explicitly requests it.

## Off by default

- Browser MCP tools (`browser_navigate`, `browser_snapshot`, `browser_take_screenshot`, scroll/click automation)
- Opening a dev server solely to verify a change you can validate from source
- A visual verification loop after every code change

## On demand — use when the user asks

- User says to verify in browser, open localhost, take a screenshot, or check scroll/UI live
- User reports a visual bug that cannot be diagnosed from source alone
- User provides a screenshot — analyze it (no browser needed unless they also ask you to open one)

## Preferred workflow (when user has not asked for browser)

- User previews locally via `dev-server/start-restart-dev.bat` and shares screenshots
- For scroll-motion work: read `src/client/scroll-motion.js` and related CSS first

## When on-demand browser verification is active

- Run the check, report findings, then stop — do not leave browser automation running across unrelated tasks
